Negative control for what the page header is NOT (G3, G4, AC5.2).

Puts a display setting back in the header: the view toggle rides in beside the
title, so the cluster G4 broke apart re-forms one line higher up -- the data
action and the "how the same rows are drawn" control sharing a row again. The
title, the collection actions and the handoff they open are untouched, so what
goes red is the one claim under test: the header holds the page's own action
and nothing that only changes the display.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: page-header.spec.ts -- the AC5.2 case (the header renders no ordering or
view control; those sit on the data surface).

